
  ┌─ Logic › Loops ────────────────────────────────────── lesson · step 2/3 ─┐
  │                                                                          │
  │ A for loop repeats its body while its condition holds.                   │
  │                                                                          │
  │  1  for i := 0; i < 3; i++ {                                         go  │
  │  2      fmt.Println(i)                                                   │
  │  3  }                                                                    │
  │                                                                          │
  │ ✓ 1  i := 0 runs once, before the first check of i < 3.                  │
  │                                                                          │
  │ ▸ 2  Predict: After the loop prints 2, what happens next?                │
  │                                                                          │
  │         1   i becomes 3 and the loop stops                               │
  │       ▸ 2   It prints 3 and then stops                                   │
